<title>USA: Sprint launches oddlot share buyback plan.</title>
<headline>Sprint launches oddlot share buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp said Friday it launched a voluntary program allowing stockholders with fewer than 100 shares the option to sell their stock or purchase additional shares.</p>
<p>Sprint said the program is in response to shareholder requests. A processing fee of $0.75 a share for the sale or purchase of shares will be charged.</p>
<p>Boston EquiServ will administer the program, which expires on April 18 unless extended, Sprint said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
